<title>FRANCE: France orders Thomson-CSF helicopter drone.</title>
<headline>France orders Thomson-CSF helicopter drone.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French army has ordered an unmanned helicopter drone system for field tests from Thomson-CSF and TechnoSud Industries, Thomson-CSF said on Wednesday at the Paris air show.</p>
<p>The Vigilant F200 M helicopter unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) system consists of a ground control station and one or two unmanned helicopters equipped with a panoramic camera and a pan/tilt zoom camera, for use in reconnaissance and scouting operations. No price details were given.</p>
<p>Thomson-CSF expects several export orders before the end of the year, it said in a statement.</p>
